4. npm / Bun dependencies
   Dependencies are not vendored in this repository; they are installed from
   the lock files. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md lists the packages that the built
   UI, the compiled backend and the desktop app can contain, with the
   license each declares and the license texts of the installed copies; it
   is generated by scripts/oss/notices.mjs and is an inventory, not a legal
   review. Points that a package's license field does not show:
   - KaTeX (MIT) ships fonts that are bundled into the built UI; the fonts
     are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Their copyright lines and the
     OFL text: licenses/katex-fonts-OFL-1.1.txt.
   - Electron (MIT) contains Chromium, Node.js, FFmpeg (LGPL-2.1-or-later in
     the configuration Chromium builds) and many other components; their
     notices are in Electron's LICENSES.chromium.html, which a packaged app
     carries under Resources/licenses/electron/.
   - Bun (MIT), whose runtime is compiled into the backend executable of a
     packaged app, statically links JavaScriptCore / WebKit (LGPL-2), tinycc
     (LGPL-2.1) and other libraries under their own licenses
     (https://bun.com/docs/project/license).

